meta {
  name: WxC User: API Hang Up
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: https://webexapis.com/v1/telephony/calls/hangup
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Authorization: Bearer {{personaltoken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "callId": "Y2lzY29zcGFyazovL3VzL0NBTEwvY2FsbGhhbGYtNzEzOTEzNzg1ODow"
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Hangs up an active call on a person's personal virtual line, by Call ID — the Call Controls
  "Hangup" endpoint. (Removed a stray duplicate empty `Authorization` header that was left over
  above the real one during this documentation pass — harmless, but some HTTP clients reject
  duplicate headers outright.)

  **Parameters/Headers**
  - `Authorization` — bound to `{{personaltoken}}` (placeholder). Use a personal access token from
    the user who owns the phone. This can be copied from developer.webex.com.

  **Body** (`body:json`)
  - `callId` — the ID of the call to hang up, returned by "WxC User Phone: API Dial" (or any other
    call-creating request) when the call started.

  **Usage**: Returns a 200 OK with no response body on success.

  See https://github.com/TeamCCEP/DeskphoneControl for more info and a little web app that will
  help visualise these APIs.

  Reference: https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/call-controls/hangup

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}
